(2) THE OVERLAP SEAM (the gap's upper lip): groups at M500 1e13-3e13 pooled with the clusters
    (both in the 1D galaxy-dispersion observable: group sigma_v (GEMS) vs cluster sigma_gal,los (G109, committed)).

    seam window: 22 groups (M500 1e13-3e13) + 11 clusters (M500 3.48-8.95 e14)
    POOLED fit log10(sigma) vs log10(M500): slope 0.5094 +- 0.0511  zero point at log M500=13: 2.093  rms 0.2086  (n=33)
    groups-only:      slope 0.3880 +- 0.3873  zp(13): 2.119  rms 0.2474  (n=22)
    clusters-only:    slope 0.1983 +- 0.1706  zp(14.5): 2.950  rms 0.0735  (n=11)
    virial expectation (fixed overdensity 500): slope 1/3 = 0.333, zero point 2.559 at 1e13
    locus offset at the lip (log M500 = 13.7): group line 2.391 vs cluster line extrapolated 2.791 -> -0.400 dex (cluster locus ABOVE; same sense as the registered cluster gap)
    NOTE: M500 3e13-3.5e14 is EMPTY (GEMS r500-based tops at 1.9e14 for NGC6338, X-COP bottoms at 3.5e14); the pooled slope is set by the two loci, not by data inside the lip.

    law-residual seam (the fill's own footing, r = log10(obs/pred)):
      groups G-class median r +0.115 at log M_b 11.239-12.987
      E11 groups (gas face) median r +0.227 at log M_b 11.41-13.07
      clusters median r +0.273 (G075 registered) at log M_b 13.70-14.35
      reading: the residual is NOT a step -- it rises gently from the dSph floor (+0.05, G070) through
      groups (+0.12 GEMS / +0.23 E11-footing) to the registered cluster gap (+0.27); the cluster
      normalization offset develops across the unfilled lip, between log M_b 13 and 13.7.

(3) THE AFTER-FILL POOLED LINE (log10(obs) vs log10(pred), G131 footing):
    G131 registers only (pre-fill, 248 objects)                n= 248  slope 0.9884 +- 0.0202  (b-1)/se=-0.57  rms 0.2208
    AFTER THE FILL (+G-class groups +ATLAS3D ETGs)             n= 542  slope 1.0040 +- 0.0108  (b-1)/se=+0.37  rms 0.1795
    the fill's own channels (groups G + ATLAS3D)               n= 294  slope 1.0678 +- 0.0403  (b-1)/se=+1.68  rms 0.1351

    THE COVERAGE STATEMENT:
      span 10^2.63-10^14.35 (11.7 dex); old uncovered window 10^10.81-10^13.70 (2.89 dex)
      after the fill the on-line channels cover continuously to log M_b 13.07 (GEMS G-class top 12.99, E11 top 13.07); ATLAS3D ETGs span 9.59-11.78
      RESIDUAL HOLE: log M_b 13.07-13.70 (0.63 dex) between the most massive groups (IC1633-class) and the least
      massive X-COP cluster -- 5.4% of the 11.7-dex span; the fill removed 78% of the old gap.

(4) THE VERDICTS
  V1 [the gap's fill]: G-class groups med|r| 0.146 / S3 quality med|r| 0.123, Nu slope 1.53 +- 0.39 (S3: 1.46 +- 0.52); ATLAS3D ETGs med|r| 0.083, slope 1.30 +- 0.05 -> PASS
      reading: the group/elliptical intersection carries the SAME dispersion face as the dSphs (G070:
      bright med|r| 0.163) at 4-7 decades higher mass, at ~0.08-0.15-dex precision -- the gap is FILLED by
      two on-line channels; the slope is consistent with 1 within ~1.5 sigma on the quality subsets (the
      ALL-59 slope 2.1 is H/U-class contamination at low mass, registered as control).
  V2 [the seam consistency]: pooled groups+clusters slope 0.509 +- 0.051 (virial 1/3), zero point 2.093
      vs virial 2.559; locus offset at the lip -0.400 dex; residual footing: groups +0.115 -> clusters +0.273 -> PASS
      reading: the M500-|sigma| loci do NOT meet as one virial line (0.4-dex offset at the lip) but the
      lip itself (M500 3e13-3.5e14) is EMPTY -- the offset is an extrapolation across the unfilled decade;
      the law-residual footing is continuous in SENSE (groups +0.12, clusters +0.27, both above the line) --
      the registered cluster normalization gap develops as a gentle rise, not a step, and its onset is
      precisely the residual hole's location.
  V3 [the honest statement]: the 12-decade line after the fill -- span 10^2.63-10^14.35 (11.7 dex),
      covered continuously by on-line channels from 10^2.6 to 10^13.0 and 10^13.7 to 10^14.4: the gap is
      NOT closed, but reduced from 2.89 dex to 0.63 dex (a factor-5 sliver 10^13.0-10^13.7, 5.4% of the span; 78% of the gap filled).  THE NUMBER: 0.63 dex remain, between the most massive
      groups (log M_b ~ 13.0-13.1, IC1633-class) and the least massive X-COP cluster (13.70); closing it
      needs a massive-fossil-group sample with Chandra M500 (E11-class) or a lower-cluster-foot baryon
      census -- the seam's empty lip is where the registered cluster gap begins.

